# Source is text, and a diff is how a change is reviewed. A single stray NUL
# would otherwise make git call a file binary and print "Bin 9422 -> 9747
# bytes" where the change should be.
*.ts text diff
*.tsx text diff
*.js text diff
*.py text diff
*.md text diff
*.css text diff
*.toml text diff

# A patch keeps the context lines of the file it patches, and a blank context line is a single
# space: that is the format, not trailing whitespace.
ptyd/libghostty/patches/*.patch -whitespace

# The daemon's files are used byte for byte: its test data is compared with what its code produces,
# and its shell scripts are compiled in and written out for the shells to read. A checkout on Windows,
# where git turns line ends into CRLF by default, would change both, so nothing here is converted.
ptyd/** -text

# Signed fixtures are bytes, not text: a Windows checkout turning their line ends into CRLF changed
# the message a signature covers, and the signature no longer verified.
desktop/testdata/** -text

# The README's pictures are three quarters of the published tree, and a native installation downloads
# that tree as an archive on its first run: 84 MB, minutes on a home connection, for files nothing at
# runtime reads. GitHub still shows them in the README; only the archive leaves them out.
docs/screenshots/** export-ignore
